{"bendscript":"0.1","blocks":[{"id":"blk-37894","kind":"heading","level":1,"spans":[{"id":"spn-63503","text":"Portable Subject-Mode Closure — memo"}]},{"id":"blk-37895","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-63504","marks":["bold"],"text":"Slice:"},{"id":"spn-63505","text":" the correction ruled onto the top of the identity ladder, not a new rung. "},{"id":"spn-63506","marks":["bold"],"text":"Status:"},{"id":"spn-63507","text":" shipped."}]},{"id":"blk-37896","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-63508","marks":["bold"],"text":"Battery."},{"id":"spn-63509","text":" D31–D40 with the engine present: "},{"id":"spn-63510","marks":["bold"],"text":"10 passed / 0 skipped / 0 failed"},{"id":"spn-63511","text":"; engine absent: "},{"id":"spn-63512","marks":["bold"],"text":"4 passed / 6 skipped / 0 failed"},{"id":"spn-63513","text":" (D32, D37, D38 and D40 are recipient-side laws and need no Forge checkout — see §3). D1–D40: "},{"id":"spn-63514","marks":["bold"],"text":"40/40"},{"id":"spn-63515","text":" engine present, 16/24 engine absent. Whole tree: "},{"id":"spn-63516","marks":["bold"],"text":"474 passed / 0 skipped / 0 failed"},{"id":"spn-63517","text":" across 26 files."}]},{"id":"blk-37897","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-63518","text":"Ruled by the sixth GPT-5.6 ruling, which accepted "},{"id":"spn-63519","marks":["code"],"text":"bundle-…"},{"id":"spn-63520","text":" and then reproduced the caveat §6 of the previous memo had flagged:"}]},{"id":"blk-37898","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"source file mode:       0664\nmanifest mode:          0644\nbundle verification:    passes\ncanonical ZIP extract:  0644\nsame bundle_id:         yes          ← and yet\ndifferent snap-:        yes          ← so a different env-"},{"id":"blk-37899","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"pack directory        → bundle verifies, environment verifies\narchive-bundle        → normalizes 0664 → 0644\nextract archive       → bundle still verifies, environment FAILS to reopen"},{"id":"blk-37900","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-63521","text":"It ruled that a reachable correctness defect, not an acceptable residual, and ordered it closed now."}]},{"id":"blk-37901","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-63522","text":"1. Why the previous slice was wrong to ship it as a caveat"}]},{"id":"blk-37902","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-63523","text":"Both halves of the tension were individually correct and I could not see a way to weaken either, so I recorded the residual and moved on. That was the error. The residual is not a "},{"id":"spn-63524","marks":["italic"],"text":"tension between two identities"},{"id":"spn-63525","text":" — it is a "},{"id":"spn-63526","marks":["bold"],"text":"package that cannot survive its own archive"},{"id":"spn-63527","text":", and neither identity has to move to say so. The fix lives in a third place: "},{"id":"spn-63528","marks":["bold"],"text":"admission"},{"id":"spn-63529","text":". A mode that cannot be transported is refused before either id is minted."}]},{"id":"blk-37903","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-63530","text":"Stated the other way round: "},{"id":"spn-63531","marks":["code"],"text":"snap-…"},{"id":"spn-63532","text":" sealing the exact mode is a claim about a repository, and "},{"id":"spn-63533","marks":["code"],"text":"bundle-…"},{"id":"spn-63534","text":" carrying the canonical mode is a claim about a distribution. There is no contradiction, only a set of repositories that are not distributable. TRAAVIIS packages distributions. So that set is inadmissible."}]},{"id":"blk-37904","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-63535","text":"2. What was built"}]},{"head":[{"id":"blk-37906","spans":[{"id":"spn-63536","text":"file"}]},{"id":"blk-37907","spans":[{"id":"spn-63537","text":"change"}]}],"id":"blk-37905","kind":"table","rows":[[{"id":"blk-37908","spans":[{"id":"spn-63538","marks":["code"],"text":"traaviis/substrates.py"}]},{"id":"blk-37909","spans":[{"id":"spn-63539","marks":["code"],"text":"CANONICAL_SUBJECT_MODES"},{"id":"spn-63540","text":", "},{"id":"spn-63541","marks":["code"],"text":"canonical_subject_mode"},{"id":"spn-63542","text":", "},{"id":"spn-63543","marks":["code"],"text":"require_canonical_subject_modes"},{"id":"spn-63544","text":"; called from "},{"id":"spn-63545","marks":["bold"],"text":"both"},{"id":"spn-63546","text":" Residency seams."}]}],[{"id":"blk-37910","spans":[{"id":"spn-63547","marks":["code"],"text":"traaviis/bundle.py"}]},{"id":"blk-37911","spans":[{"id":"spn-63548","marks":["code"],"text":"write_archive"},{"id":"spn-63549","text":" gated on a serialized round trip; new "},{"id":"spn-63550","marks":["code"],"text":"_verify_serialized"},{"id":"spn-63551","text":"; new refusal "},{"id":"spn-63552","marks":["code"],"text":"BUNDLE_ARCHIVE_ROUNDTRIP"},{"id":"spn-63553","text":"; report gains "},{"id":"spn-63554","marks":["code"],"text":"roundtrip_verified"},{"id":"spn-63555","text":"."}]}],[{"id":"blk-37912","spans":[{"id":"spn-63556","marks":["code"],"text":"traaviis/scaffold.py"}]},{"id":"blk-37913","spans":[{"id":"spn-63557","marks":["code"],"text":"SCAFFOLD_FILE_MODE"},{"id":"spn-63558","text":"; every scaffolded file written at an explicit "},{"id":"spn-63559","marks":["code"],"text":"0644"},{"id":"spn-63560","text":"."}]}],[{"id":"blk-37914","spans":[{"id":"spn-63561","marks":["code"],"text":"traaviis/cli.py"}]},{"id":"blk-37915","spans":[{"id":"spn-63562","marks":["code"],"text":"eval-one"},{"id":"spn-63563","text":" relabels the legacy field "},{"id":"spn-63564","marks":["bold"],"text":"\"episode evidence\""},{"id":"spn-63565","text":"; "},{"id":"spn-63566","marks":["code"],"text":"archive-bundle"},{"id":"spn-63567","text":" prints the round-trip line."}]}],[{"id":"blk-37916","spans":[{"id":"spn-63568","marks":["code"],"text":"traaviis/evalsplit.py"}]},{"id":"blk-37917","spans":[{"id":"spn-63569","marks":["code"],"text":"EvaluationV1.bundle"},{"id":"spn-63570","text":" documented as a legacy episode-member field with a frozen value law."}]}],[{"id":"blk-37918","spans":[{"id":"spn-63571","marks":["code"],"text":"test/test_bundle.py"}]},{"id":"blk-37919","spans":[{"id":"spn-63572","text":"D31–D40."}]}],[{"id":"blk-37920","spans":[{"id":"spn-63573","marks":["code"],"text":"RFC_TRAAVIIS_ARTIFACTS.md"}]},{"id":"blk-37921","spans":[{"id":"spn-63574","text":"new "},{"id":"spn-63575","marks":["bold"],"text":"§5c"},{"id":"spn-63576","text":" freezes both laws; §5b gains the "},{"id":"spn-63577","marks":["code"],"text":"EvaluationV1.bundle"},{"id":"spn-63578","text":" paragraph."}]}],[{"id":"blk-37922","spans":[{"id":"spn-63579","marks":["code"],"text":"README.md"}]},{"id":"blk-37923","spans":[{"id":"spn-63580","text":"archive publication, a subject-mode section, and the legacy-field note."}]}]]},{"id":"blk-37924","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-63581","text":"The admission law"}]},{"id":"blk-37925","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-63582","text":"For "},{"id":"spn-63583","marks":["code"],"text":"residency.repository.v1"},{"id":"spn-63584","text":", every file whose mode enters "},{"id":"spn-63585","marks":["code"],"text":"SnapshotV1.file_modes"},{"id":"spn-63586","text":" must already be exactly "},{"id":"spn-63587","marks":["code"],"text":"0644"},{"id":"spn-63588","text":" or "},{"id":"spn-63589","marks":["code"],"text":"0755"},{"id":"spn-63590","text":":"}]},{"id":"blk-37926","kind":"code","language":"json","text":"{\"paths\": {\"src/tool.py\": {\"observed\": \"0664\", \"required\": \"0644\"}}}"},{"id":"blk-37927","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-63591","text":"typed "},{"id":"spn-63592","marks":["bold"],"text":"`SUBJECT_MODE_NONCANONICAL`"},{"id":"spn-63593","text":", raised from one shared helper called by "},{"id":"spn-63594","marks":["code"],"text":"recompute_subject_identity"},{"id":"spn-63595","text":" (authoring) and "},{"id":"spn-63596","marks":["code"],"text":"_reopen_subject"},{"id":"spn-63597","text":" (reopening, therefore also "},{"id":"spn-63598","marks":["code"],"text":"reopen_package"},{"id":"spn-63599","text":" and therefore "},{"id":"spn-63600","marks":["code"],"text":"verify_bundle"},{"id":"spn-63601","text":"). That covers all three ways a nonportable package can appear: authored here, hand-built elsewhere, or authored before the law existed."}]},{"id":"blk-37928","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-63602","text":"The helper reads "},{"id":"spn-63603","marks":["code"],"text":"SnapshotV1.file_modes"},{"id":"spn-63604","text":" rather than walking the tree. That is the whole of D35: "},{"id":"spn-63605","marks":["code"],"text":"file_modes"},{"id":"spn-63606","text":" is already post-exclusion and already symlink-free, so an excluded file is out of scope "},{"id":"spn-63607","marks":["bold"],"text":"by construction"},{"id":"spn-63608","text":" rather than by a second glob match that could drift away from the first."}]},{"id":"blk-37929","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-63609","marks":["code"],"text":"f\"{mode:04o}\""},{"id":"spn-63610","text":" renders set-ID modes as "},{"id":"spn-63611","marks":["code"],"text":"4755"},{"id":"spn-63612","text":" / "},{"id":"spn-63613","marks":["code"],"text":"2755"},{"id":"spn-63614","text":" / "},{"id":"spn-63615","marks":["code"],"text":"1644"},{"id":"spn-63616","text":", which are outside a two-element allowlist and are therefore refused without needing to be enumerated. The law is stated as an allowlist for exactly that reason."}]},{"id":"blk-37930","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-63617","text":"The archive publication law"}]},{"id":"blk-37931","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"verify source tree\n→ write a temporary archive\n→ extract it to a temporary directory\n→ verify bundle closure from the extracted bytes\n→ when not --package-only, re-derive env- and subject closure too\n→ compare bundle_id and env_id\n→ atomically publish"},{"id":"blk-37932","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-63618","text":"The old order verified the "},{"id":"spn-63619","marks":["italic"],"text":"directory"},{"id":"spn-63620","text":" and then serialized it, which proves the directory — not the artifact anyone receives. Anything serialization normalizes away was invisible to it, which is precisely how the mode defect could reach a published archive. A failed round trip raises "},{"id":"spn-63621","marks":["code"],"text":"BUNDLE_ARCHIVE_ROUNDTRIP"},{"id":"spn-63622","text":" and leaves no archive at the output path."}]},{"id":"blk-37933","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-63623","text":"3. D31–D40"}]},{"head":[{"id":"blk-37935","spans":[{"id":"spn-63624","text":"#"}]},{"id":"blk-37936","spans":[{"id":"spn-63625","text":"law"}]},{"id":"blk-37937","spans":[{"id":"spn-63626","text":"test"}]}],"id":"blk-37934","kind":"table","rows":[[{"id":"blk-37938","spans":[{"id":"spn-63627","text":"D31"}]},{"id":"blk-37939","spans":[{"id":"spn-63628","text":"a Residency subject mode "},{"id":"spn-63629","marks":["code"],"text":"0664"},{"id":"spn-63630","text":" is refused"}]},{"id":"blk-37940","spans":[{"id":"spn-63631","marks":["code"],"text":"test_d31_a_noncanonical_residency_subject_mode_is_refused"}]}],[{"id":"blk-37941","spans":[{"id":"spn-63632","text":"D32"}]},{"id":"blk-37942","spans":[{"id":"spn-63633","marks":["code"],"text":"0600"},{"id":"spn-63634","text":" / "},{"id":"spn-63635","marks":["code"],"text":"0640"},{"id":"spn-63636","text":" / "},{"id":"spn-63637","marks":["code"],"text":"0775"},{"id":"spn-63638","text":" / set-ID modes are refused too"}]},{"id":"blk-37943","spans":[{"id":"spn-63639","marks":["code"],"text":"test_d32_every_other_noncanonical_mode_is_refused_too"}]}],[{"id":"blk-37944","spans":[{"id":"spn-63640","text":"D33"}]},{"id":"blk-37945","spans":[{"id":"spn-63641","text":"canonical "},{"id":"spn-63642","marks":["code"],"text":"0644"},{"id":"spn-63643","text":" subjects survive directory→ZIP→extract→verify"}]},{"id":"blk-37946","spans":[{"id":"spn-63644","marks":["code"],"text":"test_d33_canonical_0644_subjects_survive_directory_zip_extract_verify"}]}],[{"id":"blk-37947","spans":[{"id":"spn-63645","text":"D34"}]},{"id":"blk-37948","spans":[{"id":"spn-63646","text":"canonical "},{"id":"spn-63647","marks":["code"],"text":"0755"},{"id":"spn-63648","text":" subjects survive the same path"}]},{"id":"blk-37949","spans":[{"id":"spn-63649","marks":["code"],"text":"test_d34_canonical_0755_subjects_survive_the_same_path"}]}],[{"id":"blk-37950","spans":[{"id":"spn-63650","text":"D35"}]},{"id":"blk-37951","spans":[{"id":"spn-63651","text":"excluded files' modes do not affect admission"}]},{"id":"blk-37952","spans":[{"id":"spn-63652","marks":["code"],"text":"test_d35_excluded_files_with_noncanonical_modes_do_not_affect_admission"}]}],[{"id":"blk-37953","spans":[{"id":"spn-63653","text":"D36"}]},{"id":"blk-37954","spans":[{"id":"spn-63654","text":"presentation modes may normalize without moving "},{"id":"spn-63655","marks":["code"],"text":"env-…"}]},{"id":"blk-37955","spans":[{"id":"spn-63656","marks":["code"],"text":"test_d36_presentation_modes_may_normalize_without_moving_the_environment"}]}],[{"id":"blk-37956","spans":[{"id":"spn-63657","text":"D37"}]},{"id":"blk-37957","spans":[{"id":"spn-63658","text":"publication verifies the extracted archive before rename"}]},{"id":"blk-37958","spans":[{"id":"spn-63659","marks":["code"],"text":"test_d37_archive_publication_verifies_the_extracted_archive_before_rename"}]}],[{"id":"blk-37959","spans":[{"id":"spn-63660","text":"D38"}]},{"id":"blk-37960","spans":[{"id":"spn-63661","text":"a failed round trip leaves no final archive"}]},{"id":"blk-37961","spans":[{"id":"spn-63662","marks":["code"],"text":"test_d38_a_failed_archive_roundtrip_leaves_no_final_archive"}]}],[{"id":"blk-37962","spans":[{"id":"spn-63663","text":"D39"}]},{"id":"blk-37963","spans":[{"id":"spn-63664","text":"ZIP and tar full "},{"id":"spn-63665","marks":["italic"],"text":"environment"},{"id":"spn-63666","text":" verification agree"}]},{"id":"blk-37964","spans":[{"id":"spn-63667","marks":["code"],"text":"test_d39_zip_and_tar_full_environment_verification_agree"}]}],[{"id":"blk-37965","spans":[{"id":"spn-63668","text":"D40"}]},{"id":"blk-37966","spans":[{"id":"spn-63669","text":"D1–D30 and the packet gates remain green"}]},{"id":"blk-37967","spans":[{"id":"spn-63670","marks":["code"],"text":"test_d40_the_earlier_laws_and_the_packet_gates_are_untouched"}]}]]},{"id":"blk-37968","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-63671","text":"D31 additionally proves both non-authoring seams: a hand-built package whose seal is "},{"id":"spn-63672","marks":["italic"],"text":"self-consistent"},{"id":"spn-63673","text":" at "},{"id":"spn-63674","marks":["code"],"text":"0664"},{"id":"spn-63675","text":" is refused at reopen, and a scaffold written under "},{"id":"spn-63676","marks":["code"],"text":"umask 002"},{"id":"spn-63677","text":" still packs (see §4)."}]},{"id":"blk-37969","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-63678","text":"D37 is observed at the publication seam — it spies "},{"id":"spn-63679","marks":["code"],"text":"verify_bundle"},{"id":"spn-63680","text":" and "},{"id":"spn-63681","marks":["code"],"text":"os.replace"},{"id":"spn-63682","text":" and asserts that everything verified before publication was an "},{"id":"spn-63683","marks":["bold"],"text":"extraction"},{"id":"spn-63684","text":", never the source directory. D38 drives both failure modes: a closure failure out of the extraction, and a round trip that verifies cleanly as some "},{"id":"spn-63685","marks":["italic"],"text":"other"},{"id":"spn-63686","text":" package, which is the branch that catches silent normalization."}]},{"id":"blk-37970","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-63687","text":"D40 is a completeness check, not a re-run: D1–D30 are re-run by the battery itself, in the same process, every time. What D40 asserts is that no earlier law was dropped or renamed (the D-numbers are exactly 1..40), that the source-release gate learned nothing about either new code, and that "},{"id":"spn-63688","marks":["code"],"text":"TrvmWorldV1"},{"id":"spn-63689","text":" did "},{"id":"spn-63690","marks":["bold"],"text":"not"},{"id":"spn-63691","text":" inherit the mode law while "},{"id":"spn-63692","marks":["code"],"text":"ResidencyRepositoryV1"},{"id":"spn-63693","text":" enforces it at exactly two seams."}]},{"id":"blk-37971","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-63694","text":"4. A defect this slice created and then closed"}]},{"id":"blk-37972","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-63695","text":"Adding the admission law immediately broke "},{"id":"spn-63696","marks":["code"],"text":"trvs init"},{"id":"spn-63697","text":" on any machine with a loose umask. "},{"id":"spn-63698","marks":["code"],"text":"scaffold.materialize"},{"id":"spn-63699","text":" wrote every file at the process umask default, so under "},{"id":"spn-63700","marks":["code"],"text":"umask 002"},{"id":"spn-63701","text":" a freshly scaffolded environment is "},{"id":"spn-63702","marks":["code"],"text":"0664"},{"id":"spn-63703","text":" and "},{"id":"spn-63704","marks":["code"],"text":"trvs pack"},{"id":"spn-63705","text":" now — correctly — refuses it. Every author on a "},{"id":"spn-63706","marks":["code"],"text":"002"},{"id":"spn-63707","text":" machine would have been locked out by their first two commands."}]},{"id":"blk-37973","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-63708","text":"It was invisible here only because this machine runs "},{"id":"spn-63709","marks":["code"],"text":"umask 022"},{"id":"spn-63710","text":", so the default coincided with the declared mode. Exactly the same shape as the latent defect the previous slice closed, from exactly the same cause: a template's modes are part of the template, and were being taken from the machine that unpacked it."}]},{"id":"blk-37974","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-63711","text":"Closed by writing every scaffolded file at an explicit "},{"id":"spn-63712","marks":["code"],"text":"SCAFFOLD_FILE_MODE = 0o644"},{"id":"spn-63713","text":" (and the scaffold root at "},{"id":"spn-63714","marks":["code"],"text":"0755"},{"id":"spn-63715","text":", so "},{"id":"spn-63716","marks":["code"],"text":"init"},{"id":"spn-63717","text":" under a restrictive umask does not emit a "},{"id":"spn-63718","marks":["code"],"text":"0700"},{"id":"spn-63719","text":" environment either). D31 pins it with a real "},{"id":"spn-63720","marks":["code"],"text":"os.umask(0o002)"},{"id":"spn-63721","text":" scaffold that must still pack to the reference "},{"id":"spn-63722","marks":["code"],"text":"env-…"},{"id":"spn-63723","text":"."}]},{"id":"blk-37975","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-63724","text":"5. "},{"id":"spn-63725","marks":["code"],"text":"EvaluationV1.bundle"},{"id":"spn-63726","text":" — kept, relabelled"}]},{"id":"blk-37976","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-63727","text":"Ruled: do "},{"id":"spn-63728","marks":["bold"],"text":"not"},{"id":"spn-63729","text":" rename it. Done, and the strengthened D27 reading was confirmed correct. What changed is only ambiguity:"}]},{"id":"blk-37977","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-37979","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-63730","marks":["code"],"text":"trvs eval-one"},{"id":"spn-63731","text":" prints "},{"id":"spn-63732","marks":["bold"],"text":"`episode evidence: …`"},{"id":"spn-63733","text":", on both the human and the"}]}],"id":"blk-37978","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-37980","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-63734","marks":["code"],"text":"--json"},{"id":"spn-63735","text":" stderr line. It no longer prints the word \"bundle\" for this field."}]},{"id":"blk-37981","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-37983","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-63736","marks":["code"],"text":"evalsplit.py"},{"id":"spn-63737","text":" documents it as a "},{"id":"spn-63738","marks":["bold"],"text":"legacy episode-member field"},{"id":"spn-63739","text":" with a frozen"}]}],"id":"blk-37982","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-37984","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-63740","text":"value law: "},{"id":"spn-63741","marks":["code"],"text":"null"},{"id":"spn-63742","text":", or exactly one "},{"id":"spn-63743","marks":["code"],"text":"episode-<id>"},{"id":"spn-63744","text":" directory name."}]},{"id":"blk-37985","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-37987","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-63745","text":"RFC §5b and the README say the same, and both name "},{"id":"spn-63746","marks":["code"],"text":"EvaluationV2"},{"id":"spn-63747","text":" →"}]}],"id":"blk-37986","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-37988","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-63748","marks":["code"],"text":"episode_member"},{"id":"spn-63749","text":" as the eventual rename."}]},{"id":"blk-37989","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-37991","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-63750","text":"No "},{"id":"spn-63751","marks":["code"],"text":"EvaluationV2"},{"id":"spn-63752","text":" was introduced."}]}],"id":"blk-37990","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-37992","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-63753","text":"D27 remains the enforcement: no "},{"id":"spn-63754","marks":["code"],"text":"bundle_id"},{"id":"spn-63755","text":" key and no "},{"id":"spn-63756","marks":["code"],"text":"bundle-…"},{"id":"spn-63757","text":" value anywhere, "},{"id":"spn-63758","marks":["bold"],"text":"and"},{"id":"spn-63759","text":" every surviving "},{"id":"spn-63760","marks":["code"],"text":"bundle"},{"id":"spn-63761","text":" field must hold an "},{"id":"spn-63762","marks":["code"],"text":"episode-…"},{"id":"spn-63763","text":" directory."}]},{"id":"blk-37993","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-63764","text":"6. Autonomous decisions (flagged for review)"}]},{"id":"blk-37994","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-37996","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-63765","text":"**"},{"id":"spn-63766","